Automation Workflow – Migration Orchestration

START
→ Discovery Phase
    - Scan source volumes (read-only)
    - Collect metadata (size, activity, ownership, compliance flags)
    - Update CMDB baseline

→ Classification Phase
    - Categorize data: HOT / WARM / COLD / ORPHANED 
    - Validate signals (access logs, ownership, GxP flags)
    - Escalate orphaned volumes for approval

→ Planning Phase
    - Build migration wave plan (by workload type, size, compliance)
    - Calculate transfer timing (bandwidth windows)
    - Generate cutover schedule
    - Approval in ServiceNow

→ Pre-Check Phase
    - Validate target cluster capacity
    - Confirm AWS S3 buckets / storage classes exist
    - Dry-run hash sampling
    - Abort if checks fail

→ Transfer Phase
    - Execute SnapMirror for NAS volumes
    - Execute file-level copy for SMB/DFS
    - Log progress and errors
    - Throttle concurrency if bandwidth exceeded


→ Cutover Phase
    - Freeze writes on source
    - Final sync delta
    - Switch DNS/DFS mappings
    - Validate client access
    - Update CMDB

→ Validation Phase
    - Integrity check (hash sampling)
    - Performance check (latency, throughput)
    - Compliance evidence (GxP logs)
    - Go/No-Go decision

→ Reporting Phase
    - Generate migration report (success/failure, metrics)
    - Store evidence (in ServiceNow)
    - Notify stakeholders

IF Validation = FAIL
    → Rollback Phase
        - Revert DNS/DFS mappings
        - Restore pre-cutover snapshot
        - Log incident in ServiceNow
        - Schedule re-attempt

END
